::ALG1_U01_L02_Quiz_Q24::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L02_Q24
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Evaluate -3(-8).
{
=A. 24#Correct. The product of two negative numbers is positive, and 3 x 8 = 24.
~B. -24#A negative product would result from multiplying one negative and one positive number, not two negatives.
~C. 11#This adds values instead of multiplying them.
~D. -11#This combines the values with the wrong operation and sign reasoning.
}

::ALG1_U01_L02_Quiz_Q25::
Question ID: ALG1_U01_L02_Q25
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - No primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping
Question:
Number line reference: -7, -6, -5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1. Which statement is true?
{
=A. -6 < -2#Correct. -6 is farther left than -2, so -6 is less than -2.
~B. -2 < -6#-2 is to the right of -6, so it is greater, not less.
~C. -6 > 1#Any negative number is less than a positive number.
~D. 0 < -1#Zero is to the right of -1, so zero is greater than -1.
}
